  "repeats": [],
  "notes": [
   "Page 1 covers steps 1-6 (b1-b14). The minifigure assembly on the page is not a brick build, so it is not recorded.",
   "Step 1 base is read as the single Vehicle Base 4x7 (lego-2441). Steps 2-3 add the pink grooved tiles in the recess, then the yellow and grey 2x2 plates.",
   "The small images made steps 4-6 hard to read. The exact bricks that the 1x3 bricks, mudguard, clip plates and lavender plates rest on are best guesses. The bracket, grille tile, panel with divider, wheel arch, wheels and tyres are not clearly placed on this page, so they are left out.",
   "In step 6 the lavender plate (b14) and azure panel (b13) are placed on the white 1x3 bricks.",
   "Step 7 adds the third pink 1x2 grooved tile (b15) to the front grille. I attached it to the white mudguard b8, which is a guess.",
   "Step 8 shows the finished car with the minifigure seated. The minifigure is not in the parts list, so it is not recorded. The four wheels and tyres (b16-b23) are on the base wheel pins. The page-1 pictures do not show them being added, so I assumed they were added here.",
   "Step 7's picture already shows the windscreen, grille tile, bracket, panel with divider and wheel arch. Page 1's steps didn't clearly show them being placed, so I did not record them. They stay unplaced: lego-2437, lego-2412b, lego-44728, lego-93095 and lego-60212. A reviewer should place them.",
   "Page 2 otherwise has only the ad and Clubcode artwork, which add nothing.",
   "Adds the five pieces the parts list requires and the earlier graph lacked: bracket 44728, wheel arch 60212, windscreen 2437, grille tile 2412b and divider panel 93095. All five are in the finished car in step 7/8.",
   "The booklet's small pictures don't show which step places these pieces or what they sit on. The attachments (b24-b28) are best guesses from the finished model. A reviewer should check them against the full-size booklet.",
   "This reply contains only the additions. The earlier pieces (b1-b23) and their edges stay as given."
  ]
 },
